Run started 2026-11-21T12:13:03-05:00 on kali, platform k3s

################################################################################
 THREAT: Massive denial-of-service (HTTP flood)
################################################################################
 Description   : Many requests per second from one or more sources exhaust the service (CPU, worker threads, SQLite reads).
 Why relevant  : Analytics /stats reads up to 1000 rows from storage on every call; ingestion is the only entry point for sensor data. Saturating them stops the whole pipeline for every location.
 Exploitation  : Attackers loop on an expensive, unauthenticated endpoint (/stats?limit=1000) with many parallel connections; no credentials needed.
 Monitoring    : Wazuh: JSON access log, rule 100200 per request, rule 100210 = 15 requests in 10 s from the same srcip. Prometheus: http_requests_total rate, p95 of http_request_duration_seconds, http_requests_in_progress (alerts SSLEHighRequestRate / SSLEHighP95Latency / SSLEHighConcurrentRequests).
 Action-resp.  : k3s-block (iptables raw/PREROUTING on the node, before kube-proxy) on the agent that saw the flood: DROP of the source IP for 60 s, then automatic unblock.
################################################################################

